  "title": "HTTP/3: Dissect CANCEL_PUSH, PUSH_PROMISE, GOAWAY, and MAX_PUSH_ID frames",
  "description": "Summary:\n\nImplements dissection for missing HTTP/3 control frame types specified in RFC 9114 that previously had empty TODO stubs:\n\n\\- CANCEL_PUSH (0x03): Dissects the Push ID variable-length integer.\n\n\\- PUSH_PROMISE (0x05): Dissects the Push ID variable-length integer and hands the embedded header block to dissect_http3_headers().\n\n\\- GOAWAY (0x07): Dissects the Stream ID variable-length integer.\n\n\\- MAX_PUSH_ID (0x0d): Dissects the Push ID variable-length integer.\n\nChanges:\n\n\\- Dissect the variable-length integers for Push ID and Stream ID using hf_http3_push_id and hf_http3_stream_id.\n\n\\- Append the decoded IDs to the frame item header for immediate visibility in the protocol tree.\n\n\\- Subtree header dissection for PUSH_PROMISE frames when payload length exceeds the Push ID varint size.",
